nproc: Command for fetching Numbers of Cores Available for process

//Assigning Core to the currently running Process 
syntax: taskset -pc 0(core) <PID>

//Creates New Process in the specified core
taskset -c 0(core) ./file1.out &

//Shows Attributes of Proccesses.	
ps -eo pid,cmd,class,stat,psr

//Shows the Attributes of the Particular Process Which is while1.out in the following example.
ps -eo pid,psr,class,stat,cmd,psr | grep while1.out 	

//Nice Value Change
renice -n 5(New_Nice_Value) -p 64484(PID)

//Command to change Scheduling Algo. of a Process
sudo chrt -f/-r/-o PR <PID>


ASLR : Address Space Layout Randomisation
It has three values 0,1,2
0: randomisation disabled
1: partial enabled
2: fully enabled

//Shows ASLR Value
cat /proc/sys/kernel/randomise_va_space


//Changes ASLR Value 0,1,2
sudo sysctl -w kernel.randomize_va_space=0


//Address ranges assigned to different section of the memory
cat /proc/<PID>/maps


